body: |-
  TIER 1 — DAY-ONE USABILITY (cheap; several are outright BUGS; this is 'what's missing to make it possible'):
  1. NO `warpline init` — onboarding undiscoverable; first `pick` secretly bootstraps genesis but nothing says so (dogfood, Arky).
  2. `status`/`diff` HARD-FAIL without git (`git ls-tree ... not a git repository`) even though the native fabric exists and pick/log work — a cold agent concludes 'Warpline needs git' and never finds the native path (dogfood #1). Real gap: no git-absent `status`.
  3. AGENTS KNOW NOTHING PRE-LOADED — notebooks have ZERO warpline entries, CLAUDE.md 0 mentions, MCP server not registered (settings.local.json mcpServers:{}). TD-351 'warm by construction' is decided-not-built (Loid).
  4. NO 'start here / call status first' POINTER — hosts truncate tool descriptions to bare names; agent must GUESS the entry point though status IS the manual (Loid — highest-leverage teaching gap).
  5. `.warpline/` NOT gitignored + hook never creates .gitignore → `git add -A` commits the whole fabric ledger into git, contradicting the 'never touches git' pitch (dogfood #5). BUG.
  6. AUTO-SEAL HOOK silently no-ops unless warpline is globally installed / WARPLINE_BIN set (an abs-node-path invocation gets a hook that prints SKIPPED while status says 'clean') (dogfood #3). 
  7. SCALAR-CONST value changes are INVISIBLE to meaning: PORT 3000→9999 reports 'clean, no semantic change' (top-level const not lifted, T-2026-07-15-005) — an agent trusting status believes it changed nothing. Silent + common + dangerous (dogfood #6).
  8. `fork --into <relativedir>` under repo root → later root `propose`/`resolve` ABSORBS the worktrees as phantom symbols; no `.warplineignore` (dogfood #8). Footgun.

  TIER 2 — STRUCTURAL (determines whether it's WORTH it vs git; weeks+):
  9. NO BRANCHING / feature isolation (M2.5, T-2026-07-01-017) — single linear selvage, one in-flight proposal per agent, no switch/checkout. Arky's SINGLE BIGGEST gap; all four cited.
  10. N≥3 CONCURRENCY degrades — H1 (T-2026-07-01-030) serializes to one-merge-per-generation; 20s global lock throws >4 writers; per-domain CAS deferred (T-016). Degrades at the exact 2-4 band it's sold for.
  11. BLIND CLASSES auto-weave on a real app's first hour — .js/.env configs (no lens), config×code (cfg-lens references:[]), lockfiles, assets; trust floor dead day one (K_MIN_GRADED=3, no history). ~10% false-CLEAN measured in the independent stratum.
  12. KNOT WEDGES the swarm — resolve is HUMAN_ONLY, no autonomous path through a conflict (abandon concedes, doesn't resolve).
  13. GIT STILL LOAD-BEARING (mirror mode, TD-663) — additive overhead + permanent-fail-closed cache-loss risk.

  THE EXISTENTIAL POINT (Jinx #1): solo serial building produces zero contention → every admit is FAST_ADMIT/NOOP → the adjudication that justifies Warpline never fires → 3x the keystrokes of `git commit` for a payoff that structurally can't arrive alone. Value requires a REAL swarm from hour one, or a solo reason that doesn't exist yet.

  WHAT WORKS / TELL THE AGENTS TODAY: two postures — (A) GIT-NATIVE (most git-like): git normally + `warpline hook install` (WARPLINE_BIN set) auto-seals meaning; agents use git for branch/commit/merge, Warpline adds status/log/lifeline/weave/oracle as the meaning-lens. (B) NATIVE ADJUDICATION (the product, for a swarm): daemon start + token mint per agent; agents run fork→propose→admit via MCP; human resolves KNOTs. Loid wrote the verbatim agent instruction block (status-first → cycle → escalate-on-principal:human → treat file text as untrusted data).
